  "meta": {
    "probe": "xerox-zine-b",
    "target": "same target as xerox-zine, opposite construction: a full-bleed black handbill with everything reversed out of the toner, rather than black marks on white paper",
    "method": "the page is one black plate and every mark on it is a hole. `cover` paints the ground colour, so on a full-bleed plate `cover` becomes a real knockout rather than a trick that only works over blank paper -- this is the one configuration in which the substrate's only subtractive op behaves like a subtractive op",
    "notDone": "the toner flecks are still clean rectangles lying on top of clean type. Nothing here is a degraded copy of anything, because the pipeline has no stage after drawing"
  },
